WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.474 --> 00:00:02.121
(audience cheering)

00:00:02.121 --> 00:00:02.954
- Ah!

00:00:02.954 --> 00:00:03.787
- Have y'all met before?

00:00:03.787 --> 00:00:05.251
- No. Never.
- No. Nice to meet you.

00:00:05.251 --> 00:00:06.270
- And congrats!
- Nice to meet you.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.410
Thank you very much.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.570
- This doesn't even mean
anything, but you have great hair.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:10.403
- Oh, thank you.

00:00:10.403 --> 00:00:11.236
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:11.236 --> 00:00:12.250
I just like, you walked out
here, and I was like, "Okay."

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.620
Yeah, yeah.
(Gabriel laughs)

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:14.760
I don't even know if you're talented,

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.166
I'm just saying I'm gonna
start with your hair.

00:00:16.166 --> 00:00:16.999
(Gabriel laughs)

00:00:16.999 --> 00:00:18.600
So, in the movie,

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.490
Steven Spielberg directs
you playing a version

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.690
of Steven Spielberg.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.332
Wow! That had to be intimidating.

00:00:23.332 --> 00:00:24.165
(Amy chuckles)

00:00:24.165 --> 00:00:25.980
Did you get to spend any time with him?

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.000
'Cause I know, didn't y'all shoot this,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.230
some during COVID times?

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:29.760
Like when you had to,
kind of, be separate?

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.850
- We spent a lot of
time Zooming beforehand,

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.950
'cause everything that
happens to my character,

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.060
happened to him.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:36.893
- Yeah.
- And so,

00:00:36.893 --> 00:00:38.940
I wanted to understand what
story he wanted to tell.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.537
So that just meant getting to know him.

00:00:40.537 --> 00:00:42.450
- Yeah!
- And I could

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.600
just ask him questions about
his life, and get to know him.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.470
- [Kelly] That's kinda cool.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:47.370
- That was really cool.
- Just getting to sit

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.203
with Steven Spielberg,

00:00:48.203 --> 00:00:49.363
- And be like, "So?"
- Oh, yeah!

00:00:49.363 --> 00:00:50.196
- Yeah.
(Gabriel laughs)

00:00:50.196 --> 00:00:51.029
That's kinda really cool,

00:00:51.029 --> 00:00:51.862
- Just getting to know him-
- No, it was amazing.

00:00:51.862 --> 00:00:53.640
- As a human, 'cause he's so magnificent.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.440
- Oh, and he's a great guy.
- Yeah.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:56.610
- That's what I love-
- Oh, that's cool!

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.917
- Finding out about him,
that he is not just this-

00:00:59.917 --> 00:01:00.988
"Yeah, I did E.T."

00:01:00.988 --> 00:01:02.910
(Amy and Kelly laugh)
He's great.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:03.810
- No big deal.
- Yeah.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.580
- He's a really good person.
- Yeah.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.413
I love it.

00:01:06.413 --> 00:01:07.710
So, did you feel any pressure?

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.030
'Cause it's like one thing,

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.680
you wanna impress people
that have this script

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.900
and whatever character you're
playing to be impressive,

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:13.733
in that sense.

00:01:13.733 --> 00:01:15.143
But to play someone who's directing you,

00:01:15.143 --> 00:01:18.120
- Mm hmm!
- And is such a huge icon,-

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.680
- You know, in this industry.
- Yeah!

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.820
- [Kelly] Did you feel
pressure 'cause of that?

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:21.653
- Oh, yeah!

00:01:21.653 --> 00:01:23.906
You don't want to be the guy
who ruins his life story.

00:01:23.906 --> 00:01:24.773
(Amy and Kelly laughing)
Like, you don't, you know.

00:01:25.633 --> 00:01:27.510
- I love how you said it.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.610
- Yeah. That would be horrible.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:33.510
And just the ensemble
of people around you.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:34.860
- Michelle and Paul,
- Yeah!

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.560
- And Steven and Tony and Kristie,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:38.550
And even just, everyone.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:42.180
Like, you're surrounded
by masters the whole time.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.250
Even the A camera operator, Mitch;

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.500
he's stormed the beaches of Normandy

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.870
with a handheld camera
for Saving Private Ryan.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.220
- Yeah!
- Everywhere around you

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.930
are just the best of the best.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:53.640
- And,
- Opportunity!

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:54.473
What a cool one, yeah.

00:01:54.473 --> 00:01:55.740
- You wanna keep up.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.150
- So is it true though,

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.190
that you were once in a stage version,

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:00.023
I love this,
(Amy chuckles)

00:02:00.023 --> 00:02:01.590
of "Bill and Ted's Excellent Adventure?"

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.050
- Yeah, that was the play we did

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.310
in my senior year of high school.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.478
- I love that-
- Way to go!

00:02:06.478 --> 00:02:07.475
- What a cool school!
- This is a play.

00:02:07.475 --> 00:02:09.030
- Oh, yeah.
- I know!

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:09.863
Our's were like...

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:10.830
I mean, they were fine,

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.140
but they were the classic ones
that everybody always does.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.940
I just thought that was
very progressive and cool.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.560
- Oh, well it was...

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.870
I didn't take the drama class,

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.340
but the kids who did,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.820
their assignment was to write
this play, and adapt a play,

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:27.030
and they chose "Bill and
Ted's Excellent Adventure."

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:29.910
- Oh!
- And so one of my friends

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:33.367
from football and rugby, MC, he was like,

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:36.480
"Yeah, I'm writing it.
Come, audition to be Bill."

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.520
and like, "Let's audition
together as Bill and Ted",

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.780
and we did and we both got it.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:40.620
- Oh my gosh!

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:42.092
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Oh, that sounds so fun.

00:02:42.092 --> 00:02:42.925
- It was a lot of fun.

00:02:42.925 --> 00:02:44.580
- I know, this is not a joke,

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.270
I literally learned
certain historical figures

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.020
(Amy laughs)

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.319
- From that movie.
- Yeah.

00:02:50.319 --> 00:02:51.152
(audience laughing)

00:02:51.152 --> 00:02:51.985
- We'll take education-

00:02:51.985 --> 00:02:53.292
- Wherever we can get it.
- I was like,

00:02:53.292 --> 00:02:55.530
look, before Hamilton came around,

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:56.820
I was learning from Bill and Ted.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.170
- Yep! Socrates.
- Oh, yeah.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.160
- It's entertaining,

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.020
and something historical
you're learning about.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:04.140
So, what's the strangest
play you've ever done?

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:05.790
- Wow! God, that's a good question.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.754
I feel like I was a snowflake.

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:09.587
(Kelly laughs)
You know?

00:03:09.587 --> 00:03:11.040
- Oh, wow!
- In second or third grade.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.450
And she didn't really have an arc.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:13.283
We don't know

00:03:13.283 --> 00:03:15.370
what her character was.
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:16.230
It was a mess.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.610
- Well, hey, there are no small parts.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:18.810
They're the only small actors.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:19.643
- That's right.

00:03:19.643 --> 00:03:20.795
- Gabriel understands.
- Oh, okay. I like that.

00:03:20.795 --> 00:03:21.900
- That's true.
- Is that a thing people say?

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.040
- I've never heard that.
- Yes.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:23.873
- Oh!
(Gabriel laughs)

00:03:23.873 --> 00:03:24.960
- I'm not an actor.
- They usually say it

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.365
to the people that have small parts.

00:03:26.365 --> 00:03:29.448
(all three laughing)

